WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.551
Moccasin represents the schedule with retention intervals.

00:00:03.631 --> 00:00:05.241
For each node in the graph,

00:00:05.321 --> 00:00:09.059
the method allows up to a small constant number of
intervals,

00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:13.191
each specified by an integer start event and an
integer end event,

00:00:13.271 --> 00:00:18.574
indicating when that node's output tensor is
computed and how long it stays in memory.

00:00:18.654 --> 00:00:22.455
A Boolean flag marks whether each interval is
actually active,

00:00:22.535 --> 00:00:26.023
so a node need not be recomputed a fixed number of times.

00:00:26.103 --> 00:00:28.715
The objective minimizes the total duration,

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:34.286
a weighted sum over the active compute events where
the weights are node execution times.

00:00:34.366 --> 00:00:39.732
The memory budget is enforced through the
constraint programming cumulative constraint,

00:00:39.812 --> 00:00:44.051
treating tensor sizes as resource demands and the
budget as capacity,

00:00:44.131 --> 00:00:50.436
while data dependencies between predecessors and
successors are handled with the reservoir constraint.

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:54.192
The whole model is handed to Google OR-Tools'
CP-SAT solver.

00:00:54.272 --> 00:00:58.261
Because each node uses only a small constant number
of intervals,

00:00:58.341 --> 00:01:02.580
the total number of integer variables stays linear
in the graph size.
